OL,3,GNEWSANurse Sandie Peggie to appeal
OL,4,Aafter losing discrimination case
OL,5,Aagainst union
OL,6,
OL,7,FNurse Sandie Peggie is to appeal
OL,8,Fagainst the decision that she was not
OL,9,Fdiscriminated against by her trade
OL,10,Funion over her beliefs on biological
OL,11,Fsex and gender.
OL,13,FPeggie alleged the Royal College of
OL,14,FNursing (RCN) had failed to adequately
OL,15,Fsupport her during a dispute with NHS
OL,16,FFife and Dr Beth Upton.
OL,18,FThe RCN disputed the claim, arguing
OL,19,Fthat it had acted "reasonably"
OL,20,Fthroughout the process - and that view
OL,21,Fwas backed by an employment tribunal
OL,22,Fruling earlier this month.
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,429,420,260,160,0,100
